# cuttle stealth-chromium patch #57 - WebRTC candidates at --fingerprint-webrtc-ip.
#
# Source: chromium 154.0.8037.57 (ungoogled-chromium applied)
#   third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc
#   third_party/blink/renderer/platform/p2p/ipc_socket_factory.cc
#   third_party/webrtc/p2p/base/port.cc
#   third_party/webrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.cc
#
# Based on Clearcote's 100-webrtc-leak (notice below). Changes from it: the host
# candidate becomes a .local name instead of being dropped, the forced IP is
# read from cuttle's own switch, ICE-TCP and TURN over UDP are disabled, every
# UDPPort send is swallowed, and port.h is left alone (the accessors are
# declared extern by their callers).
#
# Before this patch the switch was forwarded to renderers (0050) and read by
# nothing, and ungoogled's default-webrtc-ip-handling-policy.patch makes
# disable_non_proxied_udp the default preference, so every seed gathered zero
# candidates. With --fingerprint-webrtc-ip=<ip> a page now sees what Chrome
# shows without a camera or microphone grant: one host candidate on the default
# route named <uuid>.local, and one srflx at <ip> with raddr 0.0.0.0:0. The
# forced IP overrides whatever policy is in effect. No UDP packet leaves the
# real interface: the srflx is fabricated without a STUN request, and UDPPort
# drops every send, so a direct connectivity check never reaches a peer. That
# is observable: a page's own STUN server receives no binding request (Chrome
# sends four to a silent one) yet a srflx appears. Media still connects through
# a TURN server over TCP or TLS, which Chrome dials through its proxy, as
# disable_non_proxied_udp allows; with no such server it cannot connect.
# WebRTC's own DNS lookups (a TURN hostname, a page-supplied hostname
# candidate) fail instead of reaching the system resolver outside the proxy,
# so TURN dials the hostname through the proxy.
# --fingerprint-webrtc-no-local-dns fails those lookups without a forced IP.
# Without either switch nothing changes.
#
# third_party/webrtc is a git submodule of src/. git apply run from src/
# reaches its files; only its own reset (Stage 3's submodule foreach) reverts
# them.
